<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Donna Lee" spTempo="205">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1947
Composer:	Charlie Parker*
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	32-bar AABA
Key:	Ab major

“Donna Lee” is a bebop contrafact based on the
chord progression of “Back Home Again in Indiana.”
It was recorded by Charlie Parker’s quintet in 1947.
The composition is officially credited to Parker,
although Miles Davis later claimed that he wrote
the tune—so the authorship remains disputed.</spComments>
